.TH PITBOARD-APP 1 "" "Pitboard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pitboard-app \- switch AI coding tools between your accounts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pitboard-app
.RI [ option ]
.RI [ link ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pitboard-app
is Pitboard's desktop app.
It switches Claude Code and OpenAI's Codex CLI between your own accounts without signing you
out, and shows what each account has left of its limits.
.PP
One copy runs in a session: starting it again, from the launcher, a link or a desktop action,
hands the request to that copy.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I link
Opens a
.B pitboard://
link, as the launcher does for a link the desktop hands it.
.TP
.B \-\-add\-account
Opens Add Account.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Reads every account's limits again.
.TP
.B \-\-sign\-in
Starts the app without a window, as the start at sign-in does.
.TP
.B \-\-gapplication\-service
Waits on the session bus for a request, as D-Bus activation starts the app.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Lists the options.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pitboard (1)
